' Casper change map for order-then-execute on cost-accounted (v6) shards.
' Five groups, from left to right: the Casper core that stays unchanged,
' shared code that gets a v6 branch, v6-only machinery, the cost-accounting
' modules that are designed but not yet implemented, and dev's legacy path that legacy shards keep
' byte for byte. Each element names its files. The risk of each change is in
' brackets: [H] high, [M] medium, [L] low.
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-consensus-proposal.md §8.
' Palette: unchanged Casper core = capability indigo · shared code with a v6
'   branch = control amber · v6-only machinery = pool green · cost-accounting
'   modules = gate teal · v6 merge rule retired at Phase 3 = surface salmon ·
'   legacy path kept for legacy shards = note grey
' The legend also defines every name and abbreviation that the labels use,
' so the diagram reads on its own.
' Render:  ./render.sh consensus-proposal-change-map.puml

@startuml consensus-proposal-change-map
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #333333
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #444444
}
skinparam ArrowColor $ca_neutral
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 60
left to right direction
title Casper change map for order-then-execute on v6 shards

package "1. Unchanged Casper core" as CORE $ca_pkg_indigo {
  component "Signed blocks, justifications,\nsequence numbers\nCasperMessage.proto:290-302" as BLK $ca_capability
  component "LMD-GHOST fork choice\nwith the invalid-message filter\nestimator.rs" as FC $ca_capability
  component "Equivocation detection\nvalidation_dispatcher.rs:307-316" as EQ $ca_capability
  component "Clique-oracle\ndecision rule\nclique_oracle.rs" as CO $ca_capability
}

package "2. Shared code that gets a v6 branch" as SHARED $ca_pkg_amber {
  component "[H] Block body for v6:\nenvelopes, attested root\nCasperMessage.proto:554-575, 597-605" as BODY $ca_control
  component "[H] Epoch validator set,\nequivocators weigh zero at once\nclique_oracle.rs:202-253\nblock_metadata.rs:141-162" as WEIGHT $ca_control
  component "[H] Finality hook that\nfeeds the executor\nfinalization_runner.rs:351-560\nblock_dag_key_value_storage.rs:1574-1640" as HOOK $ca_control
  component "[H] LFB containment by\nDAG ancestry on v6\nfloor.rs:615-638" as FLOOR $ca_control
  component "[M] Deploy status, exploratory\nreads, state sync from\nattested roots (node API, LFS)" as API $ca_control
}

package "3. v6-only machinery" as V6 $ca_pkg_green {
  component "[H] Proposal without execution\nblock_creator.rs\ninterpreter_util.rs:893-1030" as PROP $ca_pool
  component "[H] Structural validation,\nno merge, no replay\nvalidation_dispatcher.rs:84-334\ninterpreter_util.rs:400-555" as VAL $ca_pool
  component "[H] Linearizer:\nmain-chain epochs" as LIN $ca_pool
  component "[H] Executor after finality\nwith the P1 gate\nruntime.rs, runtime_manager.rs" as EXE $ca_pool
  component "[L] Parallel batch executor\nruntime.rs, runtime_manager.rs\ndeterministic_reduction.rs" as PAR $ca_pool
  component "[M] Attestation check\nand slashing evidence" as ATT $ca_pool
}

package "4. Cost-accounting modules, designed, not yet implemented" as CA {
  component "[L] G1 DR-64 check\nbefore execution\nruntime.rs:359-640\nexecution.rs:272" as G1 $ca_gate
  component "[L] G2 ordered batch\nof offers\nblock_creator.rs:1847-1929\nruntime_manager.rs:1737-1741" as G2 $ca_gate
  component "[L] G3 installer funding\nfamily_selection.rs:163-186" as G3 $ca_gate
  component "[L] Cost-cursor lock fix\npgmcp bug 11004\nSystemVault.rho:52-167" as R11004 $ca_gate
  component "[M] v6 merge rule DR-120\ninterpreter_util.rs, dag_merger.rs\nretired on v6 at Phase 3" as G9 $ca_surface
}

package "5. Legacy path, kept for legacy shards" as LEG $ca_note_grey {
  component "compute_parents_post_state\nand the merger\ninterpreter_util.rs:1212\ndag_merger.rs:820\nconflict_set_merger.rs:864-974" as MERGE $ca_note_grey
  component "Replay before\nacceptance\ninterpreter_util.rs:538-545" as REPLAY $ca_note_grey
}

' Order the groups from left to right.
CORE -[hidden]-> SHARED
SHARED -[hidden]-> V6
V6 -[hidden]-> CA
CA -[hidden]-> LEG

BLK --> BODY : v6 blocks carry envelopes
FC --> WEIGHT : reads weights
CO --> WEIGHT : reads weights
EQ --> WEIGHT : equivocators weigh zero
HOOK --> LIN : newly finalized set
BODY <-- PROP : filled by
FLOOR <-- VAL : uses
LIN --> EXE : canonical order
EXE <-- PAR : same result as\nsequential order
EXE --> ATT : executed roots
BODY <-- ATT : attestation field
API ..> ATT : reads attested roots
EXE <-- G1 : the P1 gate
EXE <-- G2 : batch API
EXE <-- G3 : eligible sources
PAR <-- R11004 : no global\nsettlement lock
G9 ..> MERGE : v6 seam below\ndev's dispatcher

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_capability>| unchanged Casper core |
  |<$ca_control>| shared code that gets a v6 branch |
  |<$ca_pool>| new v6-only machinery |
  |<$ca_gate>| cost-accounting modules, designed, not yet implemented |
  |<$ca_surface>| v6 merge rule, retired on v6 at Phase 3 |
  |<$ca_note_grey>| dev's legacy path, unchanged for legacy shards |
  | [H] [M] [L] | risk of the change: high, medium, low |

  |= name |= meaning |
  | v6 | protocol version 6, with cost accounting |
  | G1, G2, G3 | gap labels of epic 8946 in pgmcp, the work tracker. Each box names the work. |
  | DR-64 | the decision record of the funding check before execution |
  | DR-120 | the planned decision record of the v6 merge rule |
  | pgmcp bug 11004 | the global cost-cursor lock bug |
  | P1 gate | the acceptance gate of the paper P1, "Cost-Accounted Rho Calculus": supply must cover demand before execution |
  | Phase 3 | the order-then-execute phase of the plan |
  | LFB, LFS | the last finalized block, and last-finalized-state synchronization |
  | API, DAG | application programming interface, and the directed acyclic graph of blocks |
  | LMD-GHOST | latest-message-driven greedy heaviest-observed subtree fork choice |
endlegend

@enduml
